    "gaps": [
      "The declared type of a wrapped property is carried by definition.type_candidate, a carrier folded onto the declaration as an attribute, and an attribute is write-only to the overlay. Several reference.type mentions lie inside one property declaration -- the wrapper and the written type -- and nothing distinguishes them, so @StateObject var model = CartModel() cannot be linked to the ObservableModel it observes.",
      "No Pack publishes call arguments, so the title of .navigationTitle(\"Cart\"), the destination of a NavigationLink and the binding behind .sheet(isPresented:) are not stated. A presentation is recorded by its modifier, not by what it presents.",
      "extension Foo: View declares no definition.swift_type -- the Pack states an extension as relation.depends -- so a conformance added in an extension is not attributed to a view.",
      "A child view constructed outside var body, in a helper computed property or a @ViewBuilder function, is not a render edge, because only the body property is joined.",
      "Cross-file render edges resolve by view name, not by resolved path: nothing ties a constructor call to the module that declares the type."
    ]
